      "content": "hey, i've been tracking some stuff about my daily routine lately and the numbers are kinda weird. i realized i only need about 3-4 hours of sleep to feel completely sharp, like fully charged. also, i've noticed i can process complex info or read through docs way faster than the people i work with, almost like my brain is skipping the \"processing\" delay. it feels like i'm just operating on a different frequency or something. do you think there are specific human biological models or evolutionary subsets that show this kind of anomalous efficiency, or is this just something unusual?",
